.TH MEDIAAR 1
.SH NAME
Mediaar \- Manage your media
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmediaar\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage your media
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<LANG>\fR
UI language (e.g. en, es). Overrides the persisted toggle and system locale.
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBdesktop\fR
Start the desktop app
.TP
\fBtui\fR
Start the tui app
.SH "MEDIAAR DESKTOP"
Start the desktop app
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR mediaar desktop [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "MEDIAAR TUI"
Start the tui app
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR mediaar tui [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH CONFIGURATION
Read from the following, in ascending precedence:
.RS 4
.PP
$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/mediaar/config.toml
.PP
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mediaar/config.toml
.RE
.PP
\fBlang\fR
.RS 4
UI language (e.g. en, es)
.PP
type: string; optional: true; default: from LANG / system, else en; set with: \-\-lang
.RE
